WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:05.863
The biggest AI delivery vehicle
in Microsoft is Office 365.

00:00:05.863 --> 00:00:09.748
With a total of 150 million
monthly active users,

00:00:09.748 --> 00:00:14.748
it's really a key part of
everyday AI, we are working on.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:17.940
So I'm gonna invite my colleague
Rob to come up to show

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.190
you some cool features,
what we do with AI in Office.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:21.690
Rob?

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:23.380
&gt;&gt; Thank you, Harry.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:25.673
Hi, everybody.

00:00:25.673 --> 00:00:28.951
I'm Rob Howard, I work in the
Office product marketing team.

00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:31.671
And I'm really excited to be
here today to talk to you about

00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:34.391
the AI powered tools we're
adding to Office to help people

00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:36.340
do their best work.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.889
Now, truth is, we've actually
used AI in Office for

00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:39.519
many years.

00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:43.316
You can think of features like,
spell check and flash fill, and

00:00:43.316 --> 00:00:46.903
recommended charts that are a
standard part of the Office you

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:47.836
know and love.

00:00:47.836 --> 00:00:51.758
But with the advent of Office
365, when we took the cloud and

00:00:51.758 --> 00:00:55.162
deeply integrated it with
all the apps across Office,

00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:57.826
it really accelerated
our progress in AI.

00:00:57.826 --> 00:00:59.689
And as Office 365 has grown,

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:02.242
it's become one of our
biggest vehicles for

00:01:02.242 --> 00:01:05.354
delivering Microsoft AI
technology to real people.

00:01:05.354 --> 00:01:07.607
And helping them get
real value out of it.

00:01:07.607 --> 00:01:11.455
You'll see how we're using that
world data, user data, and

00:01:11.455 --> 00:01:14.563
especially, work data to
help save people time,

00:01:14.563 --> 00:01:18.115
to help them focus on the things
that matter most to them.

00:01:18.115 --> 00:01:20.506
Even help them be
better writers and

00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:23.143
unlock hidden insights
in their data.

00:01:23.143 --> 00:01:26.457
I'm gonna start off by showing
you four of by favorite AI

00:01:26.457 --> 00:01:28.227
powered features in Office.

00:01:28.227 --> 00:01:30.254
These are features
that I use every day.

00:01:30.254 --> 00:01:32.980
And you may have seen some of
them, but like any good AI,

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.810
they've gotten better as
more people have used them.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.116
And I wanna share
with you the latest.

00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:40.540
And then, I'm gonna show you
four new ways we're bringing

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.340
AI into Office in
the coming months.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.980
So let's get started here in
the latest version of PowerPoint

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.190
available as part of my
Office 365 subscription.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.660
I'm working on
a presentation for

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.730
the Contoso Mark 8 quadcopter.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.500
And I will tell you,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.750
I've spent most of my
career as an engineer.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.680
So actually building
impactful presentations

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.880
takes more time and
effort than I'd like.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.540
And just a second
to come back up.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.190
So building impactful

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.390
