When you move teams or
work with different groups,

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.330
it can be a barrier
to understanding.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.320
And we're now connecting Word
Online deeply with the Microsoft

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.870
graph and
the work knowledge that it has.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:18.380
So that when I open a document
like this, Word Online can use

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.260
that knowledge, pulling from the
emails that I have access to and

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.980
the documents I have access to,

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:26.400
to automatically identify
acronyms in the document.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.620
And then within the tool
I'm already using,

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:29.960
identify them for me.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.890
So I can see AINR means
Artificial Intelligence and

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.350
Research, and
that it was found from my email.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:38.300
Where I can see things like NPS
means Net Promoter Score and

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.130
it's founded from files
that I have access to

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.970
in my organization.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:44.560
If I have one of these that I
still don't quite understand,

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.390
I see BPO means
Business Planning and

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.890
Organization but
what exactly is that?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.807
I can even see exactly the
source of the information and

00:12:51.807 --> 00:12:54.790
get an excerpt to understand
that Business Planning and

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.147
Operation is actually
a team at Microsoft.

